From: Anaconda Recipes
Subject: [PATCH] Use -std=c++20 for nvcc on CUDA >= 13

pytorch 2.14 requires C++20 to compile against its ATen/torch headers.
DeepSpeed's CUDAOpBuilder.nvcc_args() picks the nvcc C++ standard from the
CUDA version and only grants c++20 for CUDA 12.5+, falling back to c++17 for
CUDA 13.x. That makes the CUDA 13.0 op build fail with
"#error C++20 or later compatible compiler is required to use ATen".
Extend the c++20 branch to CUDA >= 13 (cxx_args() is already torch-version
gated to c++20 for torch >= 2.12).

The DeepSpeed sdist contains two copies of op_builder/builder.py — one at the
repo root (used at build time) and one inside deepspeed/ops/op_builder/ (used
at runtime / packaged into the wheel). Patch both.

--- a/op_builder/builder.py
+++ b/op_builder/builder.py
@@ -890,7 +890,7 @@
 
             cuda_major, cuda_minor = installed_cuda_version()
             if cuda_major > 10:
-                if cuda_major == 12 and cuda_minor >= 5:
+                if (cuda_major == 12 and cuda_minor >= 5) or cuda_major >= 13:
                     std_lib = '-std=c++20'
                 else:
                     std_lib = '-std=c++17'
--- a/deepspeed/ops/op_builder/builder.py
+++ b/deepspeed/ops/op_builder/builder.py
@@ -890,7 +890,7 @@
 
             cuda_major, cuda_minor = installed_cuda_version()
             if cuda_major > 10:
-                if cuda_major == 12 and cuda_minor >= 5:
+                if (cuda_major == 12 and cuda_minor >= 5) or cuda_major >= 13:
                     std_lib = '-std=c++20'
                 else:
                     std_lib = '-std=c++17'
